  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: dbb49fad961c6fc499556ebf541d44f4, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: School, on Lenina Street. Lots of empty desks today. I looked after the little ones at recess.
    midDaysAnswer: School. Only four of us came. The teacher sent us home early because the rain was black.
    finalDaysAnswer: The census hall. A lady wrote my name in a big book. I told her my dolls' names too, so they get counted.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: School, on Pushkin Street. I've gone there since first grade. It's always very quiet.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My papa's flat. I stay with him on weekdays now, and with Mama on Sundays.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: From work. I help at the bread factory now that I'm fifteen.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: Nowhere. I've always been here. Haven't I always been here?
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: The place with the long shadow. It told me to come and see you.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: I don't remember coming. I just... arrived. Like the ash does.
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. Loud noises hurt my ears sometimes. If I hold very still, it goes away.
    midDaysAnswer: My tummy hurts at night. Mom says it's because I don't finish my soup. I checked, no fever.
    finalDaysAnswer: I'm sleepy all the time. My dolls say that's normal now. Everybody's sleepy.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No. I never mind loud noises. I like it best when it's really, really loud.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Nothing hurts. My mom and my dad both checked me this morning.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I'm not sleepy. And I don't play pretend anymore. I'm too old for silly games.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: My skin feels like it belongs to someone bigger.
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: Sometimes my hands don't feel like mine. I put them away when that happens.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: I don't feel anything anymore. Is that bad? I think that's bad.
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Your hat is very big. Does it fall over your eyes when it rains?
    - I found a shiny stone in the dirt today. Do you want to see it?
    - Is it always this loud out here? The city sounds like it is thinking very hard.
    midDays:
    - The swings near my building move even when there is no wind. Have you seen that?
    - Why is your shadow so much longer than you are, mister?
    - The buildings are whispering. I think they are cold. They want blankets.
    finalDays:
    - I am playing hide and seek with the sun. I think I am winning.
    - My dolls told me to be polite to the officer. So. Hello.
    - Is today going to stay forever, or is tomorrow still coming?
